{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A CI repair and landing can race, allowing the PR to be recorded as landed at an older head while the repair is left out."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"state","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Delivering a CI repair permanently overwrites persisted reasons and timestamps on unrelated historical blocked landing attempts."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A check becoming red on the default branch after trigger creation can cause an unnecessary paid repair round to start."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A legitimate stop-and-report response is rejected as an empty diff, causing repeated paid attempts and losing the useful explanation in the final result."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"test","trigger":"normal","reason":"The test's truncation removes the hostile delimiter, so it passes even when delimiter escaping is disabled."}]}